.TH VI 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vi \- editeur de texte plein ecran / screen text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vi
[+N] [file...]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Modal text editor. In normal mode, motions (h j k l w b e W B E 0 ^ $ f F t T ; , % { } G gg H M L, Ctrl-F Ctrl-B Ctrl-D Ctrl-U) move the cursor; operators d c
y > < combine with motions (dw, c$, y}, dd, cc, yy, >>); x X D C s S r R J ~ p P u . edit; i a I A o O start insertion (Esc ends it).
.PP
Search with / and ? (regular expressions), n and N repeat. Ex commands start with a colon: :w :q :wq :x :q! :e :r :N :d :y :m :t :j :s/pat/rep/[g] :g/pat/cmd
:v/pat/cmd :set (nu ai ic ws) :!cmd. Ranges: N,M % . $ 'a /pat/.
.PP
Undo (u) has one level and toggles between the two states. The dot command repeats the last change. There is a single unnamed register. Lines longer than 255
bytes are split when loaded.
.SH SEE ALSO
less(1), sed(1), ed(1)
